UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 4: Add a precise detail and check the ending', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Identifying relative clauses (who, which, that) add a precise detail about a noun so readers know which person or thing is meant; endings should still answer the story’s goal.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same strategy to an unfamiliar topic or audience, then compare the effect of two different choices.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nAdd a who/which/that clause to \"The envelope sat on the shelf\" and write one past-tense verb that needs y-to-i or doubling.\n\nFEEDBACK\nExample: \"The envelope that Nia found sat on the shelf.\" Verbs: tried, dropped, planned — formed with the taught patterns.\n\nCHECK\nA dangling clause that does not clearly modify a noun confuses which person or thing is meant.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nRevise a six-sentence story ending: include two identifying relative clauses, apply two taught spelling patterns, and check the ending solves the stated goal. List the clauses and spelling changes.\n\nWrite a short reflection describing one specific revision you made and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"English","learning_intention":"Identifying relative clauses (who, which, that) add a precise detail about a noun so readers know which person or thing is meant; endings should still answer the story’s goal.","lesson_number":3,"lesson_role":"Language and spelling","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["EN2-VOCAB-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marki