e original example and locate the words or actions that support the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Check your response against the feedback: did you address the same skill and show your reasoning? If a detail is uncertain, identify what would have to be checked. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than making the answer longer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new content. Correct the meaning, not just the appearance.","title":"Transfer to an independent example"}],"title":"Year 4: Add a precise detail and check the ending","unit_number":1,"unit_title":"Narrative: suspense, point of view and voice","week":1,"week_in_unit":1,"word_challenges":null,"worked_example":"WORK THROUGH THIS\n\"The student who lost the label checked the board again.\" The clause who lost the label identifies which student. Spelling check: hurry → hurried (y to i); stop → stopped (doubling). Ending: she finds the label and pins it before visitors arrive.\n\nExplain what makes this example accurate and effective, identifying its specific wording.","worked_visuals":[{"alt":"Identifying relative clause attached to its noun.","caption":"Who/which/that adds a precise detail.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Clause</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">who lost the label</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Noun</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">the student</text></g></svg>"},{"alt":"Taught spelling pattern beside a goal-linked ending.","caption":"Detail and ending must still answer the goal.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"31